<Doc slug="safety-words">
  <p>
    Each phone works out four words from every member’s keys and the vault’s settings. If
    someone sat in the middle, or the server swapped a key, the phones show different
    words. A server gets one guess at faking them, with odds of about one in 17 trillion.
  </p>

  <h2>Steps</h2>
  <ol class="doc-steps">
    <li>Once everyone has joined, the setup shows <strong>Safety words</strong>.</li>
    <li>Read them aloud to each member on a call or in person, or compare them in a chat you trust. Every phone must show the same four words, in the same order.</li>
    <li>All the same: tap <strong>They match</strong>. Any difference: tap <strong>They don’t match</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="doc-note">Wait until every member has compared. One member who skips the check is enough for someone in the middle to go unnoticed.</p>

  <p>
    You compare safety words again when a co-signer <a href="/docs/lost-phone">moves to a new phone</a>
    without a backup: their new phone and yours must show the same words.
  </p>

  <h2>If it goes wrong</h2>
  <dl class="doc-fixes">
    <div><dt>The words don’t match</dt><dd>Stop. Tap <strong>They don’t match</strong>; no keys or funds exist yet. Start again with a new invite, shared over a channel you trust.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>“Waiting for 1 member”</dt><dd>Someone hasn’t opened Zafe since the last person joined. Ask them to.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</Doc>
